course: dictionary
lesson: 15620
title: Teary and feelings in words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Teary comes from tear, the drop of water that comes out of your eye. So teary means full of tears, or close to crying. «Her eyes were teary when she saw the old photos.» You can see the tears are coming, even if she is not sobbing.
explain: Teary can also describe something that makes people cry. «The film was so teary that the whole cinema sniffed.» Here the film is the thing that brings the tears. Ask yourself: is the word describing a person with tears, or a thing that makes people cry?
explain: Teary-eyed means with tears in your eyes, often because you are moved, happy or sad. «Grandma went teary-eyed at the wedding.» It is informal, so you will hear it in chatty talk and stories more than in formal writing.
fact: Teary means full of tears or close to crying.
fact: «Teary eyes» means eyes with tears in them.
fact: A «teary goodbye» is one where people feel sad and may cry a little.
fact: Teary can describe a thing too: a teary film makes people cry.
fact: Teary-eyed is informal and means with tears in your eyes, often from being moved, happy or sad.
exercise: «The little girl had teary eyes after she fell over.» What does teary mean here? | Covered in mud | Tired and sleepy | *Full of tears, close to crying | Very quick and fast
exercise: Ella says, «The film was so teary.» What does she mean? | The film was very long and boring | The film had lots of loud music | The film was wet from rain | *The film made people cry
exercise: Which phrase means someone has tears in their eyes because they are moved? | Loud and cheerful | Fast asleep | Hungry and cold | *Teary-eyed
test: «The teary children waved goodbye from the bus window.» What does teary describe? | The bus was very fast | *The children were close to crying | The children were playing a game | The window was dirty
test: «Grandma was teary-eyed at the school play.» What does teary-eyed mean? | She was cold and wet | *She had tears in her eyes, moved by the play | She was angry with the actors | She was asleep in her chair
exam: Which sentence uses teary to mean a thing that makes people cry? | The teary dog wagged its tail | The teary sky was bright blue | The teary girl ran to the park | *The teary film made the whole class sniff
